        ; Actually note: this handler doesn't extract DX from the saved-register
        ; block — it pushes the live DX register directly, which works because
        ; DOS_INT21_HANDLER preserves DX inside the saved frame and the handler
        ; is entered with a fresh DX of whatever the dispatcher left there. The
        ; user's actual DL value reaches CON_PUTC_OR_FCB1 via the [bp+4] arg of
        ; its own frame after the push.
